{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_result_unhandled_1.march","start_line":8,"start_col":4,"end_line":8,"end_col":30,"message":"This capability operation returns `Result((), CapError)`, which says whether it was permitted, but `()` is expected here.","code":"cap_result_unhandled","fix":{"kind":"insert","after_line":8,"text":"    ()","applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":["Handle the refusal (`match`, `let?`), or discard the result: a call on a line of its own needs nothing, and `Authority.ignore(...)` discards it anywhere else."],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
